# L §4.6 step 5: "Its question is the input's question, if it has one, otherwise x at k: no value for <period>, the
# period of x's time key; with no time key, x at k: no value at <law date>, and with no keys at all, x: no value at
# <law date>."  "before the first row as after the last".
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = [a, b]
input r[m in months]: int
input g[k in ks]: int
input z: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..2026-05
  known 2025-12-01
  r[*] = 1
  g[a] = 1
  z = 1

ask q1: r[2026-01], r[2026-04], r[2026-07]
ask q2: g[b], z law 2026-08-01
=== expect
q1: (?"r at 2026-01: no value for 2026-01" (r[2026-01]), 1, ?"r at 2026-07: no value for 2026-07" (r[2026-07]))
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: (?"g at b: no value at 2026-08-01" (g[b]), ?"z: no value at 2026-08-01" (z))
  law date 2026-08-01, cut 2026-12-31
